# Batch files are read by cmd.exe, which needs CRLF. Everything else stays as
# it is so a checkout on any platform produces a working launcher.
*.bat text eol=crlf
# PowerShell copes with either, but Windows tools that read these expect CRLF
# and a mixed-ending file is a needless thing to have to think about.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
